Dialogue: 0,0:00:00.50,0:00:03.93,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}This is PIXIU,
Dialogue: 0,0:00:04.01,0:00:07.45,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}a comprehensive open-source framework for financial artificial intelligence,
Dialogue: 0,0:00:07.53,0:00:10.96,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}published at NeurIPS 2023.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:11.04,0:00:14.47,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}Financial language is highly technical,
Dialogue: 0,0:00:14.55,0:00:17.99,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}yet before PIXIU there were no openly released financial large language models,
Dialogue: 0,0:00:18.07,0:00:21.50,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}no financial instruction tuning data, and no holistic evaluation benchmark.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:21.58,0:00:25.01,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}PIXIU fills all three gaps at once.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:25.09,0:00:28.53,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}It contributes FIT, the first multi-task,
Dialogue: 0,0:00:28.61,0:00:32.04,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}multi-modal financial instruction dataset with one hundred and thirty-six thousand samples;
Dialogue: 0,0:00:32.12,0:00:35.55,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}FinMA,
Dialogue: 0,0:00:35.63,0:00:39.07,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}the first openly released instruction-following financial large language model built by fine-tuning LLaMA;
Dialogue: 0,0:00:39.15,0:00:42.58,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}and FLARE,
Dialogue: 0,0:00:42.66,0:00:46.09,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}a standardized benchmark spanning financial natural language tasks and stock movement prediction.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:46.17,0:00:49.61,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}Together they let the community build, compare,
Dialogue: 0,0:00:49.69,0:00:53.12,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}and advance financial LLMs in the open.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:53.50,0:00:57.49,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}Financial technology has advanced rapidly with NLP,
Dialogue: 0,0:00:57.57,0:01:01.55,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}but the highly technical nature of financial text demands domain-specific models.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:01.63,0:01:05.62,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}Existing financial pre-trained models like finBERT and FLANG are small,
Dialogue: 0,0:01:05.70,0:01:09.69,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}below one billion parameters, limiting their generalization.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:09.77,0:01:13.76,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}The one large financial model, the fifty-billion-parameter BloombergGPT,
Dialogue: 0,0:01:13.84,0:01:17.82,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}is proprietary: neither its weights nor its training data are released,
Dialogue: 0,0:01:17.90,0:01:21.89,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}and it is not instruction-following.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:21.97,0:01:25.96,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}Critically,
Dialogue: 0,0:01:26.04,0:01:30.03,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}there are no open financial instruction datasets and no standardized benchmarks for comprehensively
Dialogue: 0,0:01:30.11,0:01:34.09,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}assessing financial LLMs. This leaves the research community without the resources needed
Dialogue: 0,0:01:34.17,0:01:38.16,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}to push financial AI forward in the open.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:38.54,0:01:42.52,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}Two gaps motivate this work.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:42.60,0:01:46.58,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}First,
Dialogue: 0,0:01:46.66,0:01:50.63,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}instruction tuning has proven essential for improving a model's zero-shot ability on downstream tasks,
Dialogue: 0,0:01:50.71,0:01:54.69,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}yet no financial instruction data exists to enable it.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:54.77,0:01:58.75,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}Second,
Dialogue: 0,0:01:58.83,0:02:02.81,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}existing financial benchmarks such as FLUE cover only natural language processing tasks.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:02.89,0:02:06.87,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}They ignore financial prediction tasks like stock movement prediction,
Dialogue: 0,0:02:06.95,0:02:10.92,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}which require exploiting both text and time-series data and are far more aligned with real-world financial scenarios.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:11.00,0:02:14.98,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}PIXIU is built to close both gaps with open resources, multi-task coverage,
Dialogue: 0,0:02:15.06,0:02:19.04,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}multi-modal data, and greater task diversity.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:19.42,0:02:21.50,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}PIXIU makes four contributions.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:21.58,0:02:23.25,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}First, it introduces FIT,
Dialogue: 0,0:02:23.33,0:02:28.55,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}the first multi-task and multi-modal instruction tuning dataset for finance,
Dialogue: 0,0:02:28.63,0:02:34.33,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}covering five tasks and nine datasets with one hundred thirty-six thousand samples.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:34.41,0:02:36.29,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}Second, it introduces FLARE,
Dialogue: 0,0:02:36.37,0:02:43.82,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}the first evaluation benchmark that includes both financial language understanding and financial prediction.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:43.90,0:02:47.59,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}Third, it introduces FinMA, the first openly released,
Dialogue: 0,0:02:47.67,0:02:51.28,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}instruction-following financial large language model,
Dialogue: 0,0:02:51.36,0:02:56.86,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}achieving state-of-the-art on three financial NLP tasks and one prediction task.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:56.94,0:03:00.35,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}Fourth, it benchmarks FinMA against existing LLMs,
Dialogue: 0,0:03:00.43,0:03:05.30,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}revealing both their superiority and their key limitations for finance.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:05.68,0:03:09.54,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}The method has three stages.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:09.62,0:03:13.48,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}First,
Dialogue: 0,0:03:13.56,0:03:17.42,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}PIXIU gathers open-released data across five financial tasks: sentiment analysis,
Dialogue: 0,0:03:17.50,0:03:21.36,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}news headline classification, named entity recognition, question answering,
Dialogue: 0,0:03:21.44,0:03:25.30,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}and stock movement prediction.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:25.38,0:03:29.24,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}Domain experts write diverse task-specific instructions for each task,
Dialogue: 0,0:03:29.32,0:03:33.17,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}which are assembled with the data samples to form the FIT instruction dataset.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:33.25,0:03:37.11,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}This data is multi-modal, spanning text, tables from financial reports,
Dialogue: 0,0:03:37.19,0:03:41.05,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}and historical stock prices as time series.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:41.13,0:03:44.99,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}Second,
Dialogue: 0,0:03:45.07,0:03:48.93,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}LLaMA checkpoints at seven and thirty billion parameters are fine-tuned on FIT with multi-task instruction tuning,
Dialogue: 0,0:03:49.01,0:03:52.87,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}producing the FinMA model family.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:52.95,0:03:56.81,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}Third, FinMA and other LLMs are evaluated on the FLARE benchmark,
Dialogue: 0,0:03:56.89,0:04:00.75,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}which unifies four financial NLP tasks with six datasets and one prediction task with three datasets.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:01.13,0:04:04.47,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}FIT, the financial instruction tuning dataset,
Dialogue: 0,0:04:04.55,0:04:11.67,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}contains one hundred thirty-six thousand instruction samples across five tasks and nine datasets.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:11.75,0:04:18.21,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}The FLARE evaluation benchmark covers four financial NLP tasks with six datasets and one
Dialogue: 0,0:04:18.29,0:04:21.63,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}financial prediction task with three datasets.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:21.71,0:04:26.23,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}Sentiment analysis uses the Financial Phrase Bank and FiQA-SA,
Dialogue: 0,0:04:26.31,0:04:30.32,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}news headline classification uses the Headline dataset,
Dialogue: 0,0:04:30.40,0:04:34.33,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}named entity recognition uses a financial NER dataset,
Dialogue: 0,0:04:34.41,0:04:37.60,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}question answering uses FinQA and ConvFinQA,
Dialogue: 0,0:04:37.68,0:04:42.35,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}and stock movement prediction uses BigData22, ACL18, and CIKM18.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:42.43,0:04:48.52,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}Each task is scored with its standard metric, such as weighted F1, entity-level F1,
Dialogue: 0,0:04:48.60,0:04:54.31,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}exact-match accuracy, and the Matthews correlation coefficient for prediction.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:54.69,0:04:59.24,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}On the FLARE benchmark,
Dialogue: 0,0:04:59.32,0:05:03.86,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}the fine-tuned FinMA models significantly outperform other large language models on most financial NLP tasks,
Dialogue: 0,0:05:03.94,0:05:08.49,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}including sentiment analysis, headline classification, and named entity recognition.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:08.57,0:05:13.11,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}For example, on the Financial Phrase Bank sentiment dataset,
Dialogue: 0,0:05:13.19,0:05:17.74,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}FinMA-30B outperforms GPT-4 by ten percent F1 and BloombergGPT by thirty-seven percent F1.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:17.82,0:05:22.36,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}This demonstrates the value of tailoring LLMs to the financial domain through instruction tuning.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:22.44,0:05:26.99,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}However,
Dialogue: 0,0:05:27.07,0:05:31.61,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}FinMA underperforms on question answering tasks that demand quantitative reasoning,
Dialogue: 0,0:05:31.69,0:05:36.24,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}a limitation inherited from LLaMA's weak mathematical ability.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:36.32,0:05:40.86,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}And across all models, stock movement prediction remains challenging,
Dialogue: 0,0:05:40.94,0:05:45.49,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}leaving clear room for future improvement.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:45.87,0:05:48.41,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}Comparing model variants is revealing.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:48.49,0:05:56.41,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}FinMA-30B shows no significantly better performance than FinMA-7B on most NLP tasks or on stock movement prediction,
Dialogue: 0,0:05:56.49,0:06:03.64,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}indicating that the quality and diversity of the instruction data matter more than sheer parameter count.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:03.72,0:06:08.75,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}Scale does help on complex quantitative question answering like ConvFinQA,
Dialogue: 0,0:06:08.83,0:06:12.61,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}mirroring LLaMA's improved math ability at larger sizes,
Dialogue: 0,0:06:12.69,0:06:14.60,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}though it still trails GPT-4.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:14.68,0:06:19.29,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}Notably, FinMA-7B-full, fine-tuned on both NLP and prediction tasks,
Dialogue: 0,0:06:19.37,0:06:25.15,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}achieves the best performance among all models on the ACL18 stock prediction dataset,
Dialogue: 0,0:06:25.23,0:06:31.08,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}highlighting the promise of task-specific instruction tuning for financial prediction.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:31.46,0:06:34.05,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}A few numbers capture PIXIU's impact.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:34.13,0:06:41.98,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}The FIT instruction dataset holds one hundred thirty-six thousand samples across five tasks and nine datasets.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:42.06,0:06:47.60,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}FinMA is built on the open LLaMA model at seven and thirty billion parameters.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:47.68,0:06:50.77,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}On the Financial Phrase Bank sentiment task,
Dialogue: 0,0:06:50.85,0:06:56.97,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}FinMA-30B exceeds GPT-4 by ten percent F1 and BloombergGPT by thirty-seven percent F1,
Dialogue: 0,0:06:57.05,0:07:00.79,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}reaching a weighted F1 around zero point eight eight.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:00.87,0:07:07.86,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}FinMA achieves state-of-the-art on three financial NLP tasks and one financial prediction dataset,
Dialogue: 0,0:07:07.94,0:07:10.38,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}all while being fully open-sourced.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:10.76,0:07:12.15,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}The takeaway is simple.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:12.23,0:07:18.49,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}PIXIU provides the financial AI community with its first fully open triad: an instruction-following
Dialogue: 0,0:07:18.57,0:07:20.48,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}financial large language model,
Dialogue: 0,0:07:20.56,0:07:25.35,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}a large multi-task instruction dataset, and a holistic evaluation benchmark.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:25.43,0:07:30.79,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}It shows that careful domain instruction tuning can let a relatively small open model
Dialogue: 0,0:07:30.87,0:07:35.14,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}beat far larger general-purpose systems on financial language tasks,
Dialogue: 0,0:07:35.22,0:07:42.70,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}while honestly exposing quantitative reasoning and stock movement prediction as the field's remaining open challenges.
